00:12:54,496 --> 00:12:56,881
is worth keeping or not at all.

234
00:12:57,417 --> 00:12:58,738
Now, thank you very much.

235
00:12:59,121 --> 00:13:01,572
This is what I have for prompt drifting.

236
00:13:01,963 --> 00:13:06,913
But please make sure whatever you do,
like once you catch anything, try to

237
00:13:06,914 --> 00:13:11,595
make it in a loop fashion, so that
way, going forward, you can run it

238
00:13:11,596 --> 00:13:16,518
against your CI and make sure you're
catching all the unwanted behaviors.

239
00:13:17,018 --> 00:13:21,566
And I know, like, we cannot make
any system perfect, but we can try

240
00:13:21,566 --> 00:13:25,390
to reach up to a point where the
system is stable enough and is not

241
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:27,872
hallucinating and is free from the drifts.

242
00:13:28,078 --> 00:13:33,026
Not all drifts are bad, but those--
some drifts are actually very bad,

243
00:13:33,099 --> 00:13:34,625
and they have some consequences.

244
00:13:34,830 --> 00:13:39,663
So our agenda is to make sure that
we are trying to catch as much--

245
00:13:39,718 --> 00:13:41,316
as many failures as possible.

246
00:13:41,546 --> 00:13:42,437
Thank you very much

